why Every Horde quest of the Wailing Caverns in one run, lead-ins included.

# The Wailing Caverns' Horde quests in one guide: Tonga Runetotem's chain from
# the Crossroads to Thunder Bluff, Ratchet's pick-ups, the druids at the
# caverns, one run, then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so
# the guide picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chains: Tonga Runetotem's 870 The Forgotten Pools -> 877 The Stagnant
# Oasis -> 880 Altered Beings -> 1489 Hamuul Runetotem -> 1490 Nara Wildmane ->
# 914 Leaders of the Fang (the four Fanglords' gems). Apothecary Zamah's 962
# Serpentbloom. Mebok Mizzyrix's 865 Raptor Horns -> 1491 Smart Drinks
# (Wailing Essence); Crane Operator Bigglefuzz's 959 Trouble at the Docks
# (Mad Magglish's port); Nalpak's 1486 Deviate Hides and Ebru's 1487 Deviate
# Eradication; Mutanus's Glowing Shard (item 10441) starts 6981 The Glowing
# Shard (Sputtervalve in Ratchet, then Falla Sagewind).
#
# Left out: nothing of the Horde's.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses inside, so their goals stand
# at the door (@46.0,36.5, The Barrens) with `group 5`. The bosses come in the
# order of the client's dungeon journal (Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, Kresh,
# Lord Pythas, Skum, Lord Serpentis, Verdan the Everliving, Mutanus the
# Devourer), not of a recorded run. Every quest goal is counted by the quest
# log, so a group that takes them in another order still gets each step
# ticked. The Serpentbloom and Mad Magglish also stand in the caves outside
# the dungeon, on the Barrens map around the door.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The Forgotten Pools' spot is the data's.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   17 to 24).
# - Lint warns that the door is more than 50 yards from the Devouring
#   Ectoplasms on the Barrens map, which drop the Wailing Essence outside too;
#   the goal stays at the door for the ectoplasms inside.

